# Marketing Pages Management (MKP-001)

**Purpose:** Cross-workspace operator-managed marketing page content with tenant isolation, workspace capability gates, and workspace-agnostic public rendering in `apps/marketing`.

**Principle:** Platform engine owns persistence and HTTP contracts. Workspace manifests declare capability and allowed page keys. `guestLanding` remains the structural gate (which sections render); MKP-001 supplies **operator-editable copy** for allowed page keys.

---

## 1. Non-goals (V1 / Phase 1)

| Item | Rationale |
| ---- | --------- |
| Full block-based page builder | Defer to Phase 2+ |
| Blog / testimonials CMS | Requires media + moderation |
| Custom slug routing (`/about`) | Phase 2 |
| Marketing session / member auth | PCMS-001 — marketing stays anonymous |
| Workspace imports in `apps/marketing` | ADR-MKT-001 |

---

## 2. Architecture layers

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
| ----- | -------- | -------------- |
| **Domain** | `apps/api/src/workspace-marketing-pages/` | CRUD, publish, module gate, audit |
| **Contracts** | `packages/marketing-pages-http-contracts/` | Zod schemas for page payloads |
| **Capability gate** | Manifest `workspaceMarketingPages` + codegen bindings | Per-workspace enablement |
| **Operator UI** | `apps/web` settings `/settings/marketing-pages` | Draft edit + publish |
| **Public render** | `apps/marketing` | Fetch published payload; fallback to i18n |
| **Structural gates** | `guestLanding` (manifest) | Section on/off — unchanged |

### WAC-001

API resolves workspace type from tenant context. No `workspaceType === "denali"` branches in platform handlers. Use `isMarketingPagesSupportedWorkspace()` from generated bindings.

---

## 3. Data model (`marketing_page_contents`)

| Column | Type | Rule |
| ------ | ---- | ---- |
| `tenant_id` | UUID | RLS scope |
| `workspace_id` | text | Workspace plugin id |
| `page_key` | text | e.g. `home-hero` |
| `locale` | text | `fa` \| `en` |
| `draft_payload` | JSON | Operator draft |
| `published_payload` | JSON | Public read |
| `published_at` | timestamptz | Set on publish |
| `updated_at` | timestamptz | |

**Unique:** `(tenant_id, workspace_id, page_key, locale)`

**RLS:** `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` with `tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid`

---

## 4. Page keys (Phase 1)

| `page_key` | Payload schema | Public surface |
| ---------- | -------------- | -------------- |
| `home-hero` | `{ lead, support, ctaPrimary }` | `HomeHero` copy override when `guestLanding.sections.hero` |

Manifest `allowedPageKeys` lists keys per workspace. Unknown keys → 404.

---

## 5. HTTP routes

| Method | Path | Auth | Behavior |
| ------ | ---- | ---- | -------- |
| GET | `/public/marketing-pages/:pageKey` | Anonymous + host tenant | Published payload only |
| GET | `/settings/marketing-pages/:pageKey` | Operator | Draft + published |
| PATCH | `/settings/marketing-pages/:pageKey` | Operator owner/admin | Save draft |
| POST | `/settings/marketing-pages/:pageKey/publish` | Operator owner/admin | Promote draft → published |

Locale: `x-tenant-locale` header or `?locale=fa`.

---

## 6. Manifest block

```json
"workspaceMarketingPages": {
  "supported": true,
  "capabilityRevision": 1,
  "defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset": true,
  "capabilities": {
    "operatorEditor": true
  },
  "allowedPageKeys": ["home-hero"]
}
```

Settings hub module id: `marketing_pages` (Denali).

---

## 7. Rendering merge rules

1. `resolveGuestLandingFeatures(pluginId)` — if `sections.hero === false`, skip hero (CMS does not force section on).
2. Fetch published `home-hero` for locale.
3. If published payload valid → override i18n strings in `HomeHero`.
4. Else → i18n defaults (`catalog.home.full.hero.*`).

---

## 8. Cache / revalidation

On publish, API calls `scheduleMarketingPagesRevalidate(tenantId)` which hits `apps/marketing/app/api/revalidate` (same hook as catalog). The route purges:

| Tag | Builder |
| --- | ------- |
| `marketing-catalog-{tenantId}` | `buildMarketingCatalogCacheTag` |
| `marketing-seo-{tenantId}` | `buildMarketingSeoCacheTag` |
| `marketing-pages-{tenantId}` | `buildMarketingPagesCacheTag` |

Public fetch (`fetchPublicMarketingHomeHero`) uses `cache: no-store` in Phase 1. Tagged fetch is reserved for Phase 1.1 when `MARKETING_PAGES_REVALIDATE_SECONDS` lands.

Env (optional, shared with catalog): `MARKETING_REVALIDATE_URL`, `MARKETING_REVALIDATE_SECRET`.

---

## 9. Verification

| Check | Command |
| ----- | ------- |
| Contracts | `pnpm --filter @app-tour/marketing-pages-http-contracts test` |
| API integration | `pnpm --filter @apps/api exec env STORAGE_DRIVER=memory NODE_ENV=test node --import tsx --test test/marketing-pages*.spec.ts` |
| Playwright smoke | `pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:smoke:marketing-pages` |
| Smoke IDs | `SMK-MKP-01` owner publish → marketing hero; `SMK-MKP-02` viewer read-only; `SMK-MKP-03` locale tabs; `SMK-MKP-04` reload persistence; `SMK-MKP-05` mobile RTL; `SMK-MKP-06` validation |

### Operator UI (Phase 1.1)

| Capability | Behavior |
| ---------- | -------- |
| Locale tabs | `fa` / `en` per `MARKETING_PAGE_LOCALES` |
| Viewer read-only | `isAdminOrOwnerRole` — banner + disabled inputs; API 403 on PATCH |
| Success feedback | `data-testid` `marketing-pages-saved-draft` / `marketing-pages-saved-published` |
| Client validation | `parseMarketingHomeHeroPayload` before save/publish; `marketing-pages-validation-error` |
| Team viewer access | `resolve-operator-marketing-pages-middleware-access` in middleware + `(app)/layout` |

---

## 10. Phased roadmap

| Phase | Scope |
| ----- | ----- |
| **1** | `home-hero` operator edit + public render (this doc) |
| **2** | Custom slugs (`/p/:slug`), FAQ block page |
| **3** | Blog, gallery CMS, `guestCrossSurfaceNav` dynamic links |
